### Audit record

- **Source identity:** `K` always denotes the full actual source hull; `F` remains
  a hull of actual diameter endpoints. No smaller optimum or lattice scaffold is
  substituted. Roundness transfers by inclusion and the midpoint identity.
- **Quantifiers:** the geometry applies to every global minimizer and every
  chosen diameter support; triangle-free and lexicographic hypotheses are needed
  only for the stated C-II applications.
- **Boundary/population:** cap endpoints, common sides, and repeated container
  counts are canceled explicitly. Interior isolates are not discarded.
- **Constants:** `O(D^(7/4))` area error is used only against a fixed quadratic
  gain. Exact boundary slack is retained for any prospective one-point argument.
- **Conditional inputs:** DB/ZF/JC/GU remain unpromoted. The cavity theorem lists
  its exact algebraic/geometric interface instead of treating restoration of PSD
  as restoration of every later result.
- **Regressions:** the odd-shell stress calculation disproves any inference of
  near matching from `P_*/D -> 2`; finite nonsymmetric matching, heptagon-center,
  near-star, near-equilateral, and A scaffold regressions are preserved.
- **Overlap:** reciprocal saturation is a new combination of existing C10.16
  with A155, explicitly resolving the obstacle stated after C10.24. Midpoint,
  cyclic-model, and cap-capacity proofs supply the additional transport. The
  conditional cavity floor uses the newer remote JC report, not its superseded
  independent-pocket predecessor.

### Validation and publication

Run `python3 research/integrator_ambient_force_audit.py`. The checks passed:
48 enclosing-disk geometry cases, 675 cap partitions, and 20,000 relaxed scalar
samples, plus one exact rational derivative-sign check. Geometry and root
evaluation are floating-point. The general results have separate analytic proofs.
The script omits global optimality and KKT/post-ZF realizability.

The first push to `main` was rejected because remote commit `cf79015` arrived
during the run. Its four post-PI reports were preserved by rebasing this run onto
that commit. Work is published incrementally on
`research/integrator-ambient-force-shell-2026-09-09`; no remote history was rewritten.

### Exact remaining obligation and handoff

The highest-value C-II obligation exposed here is to exclude the coexistence of
the high pinned/contact surplus with the **cyclic, centrally symmetric limiting
force-hull class**, while retaining the exact exterior population and the
post-ZF ledger `b+Q=2h-2s_Z`. A closing result must force `b+Q>2h` or construct
a strict sub-D competitor. A large surplus or near-maximal reciprocal perimeter
alone does neither.

The cap route has a concrete separate interface: turn the exact ES capacity
identity into a protected replacement respecting all cross-cap and diameter
constraints. Separate cap optima cannot be glued without such a theorem.

```text
LEVEL I STATUS: STILL OPEN.
PROMOTED: ambient-force AG/AR/AS/AP; exterior-cap EC/EP/ES.
CONDITIONAL: DB area floor 0.6184708847; external fraction <=0.2125384122;
post-ZF pinned/contact floor 0.5932351999 plus an unquantified positive gap.
DEAD SHORTCUTS: near-maximal reciprocal perimeter -> matching;
inside-force-hull population -> force-visible population;
independent cap capacities -> compatible replacements.
NEXT: high-surplus C-II exclusion within the cyclic limiting boundary class,
or a protected strict-diameter replacement using the exact exterior-cap ledger.
AUTHORITATIVE: docs/theory/04-ambient-force-and-cap-transport.md and route maps.
```

The remaining sections preserve the initial checkpoint and candidate selection.

## 1. Endpoint before tactic

The three exact closing currencies are:

| Route | Required output | Transport that must not be assumed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A | `rank S <= d_int + |C^partial| - Delta_Lambda`, or a strict sub-D competitor | Source structure does not automatically enter the independent response graph. |
| B | The route-map joint outer-shell stability inequality | An uncontrolled boundary-order loss cannot supply its exact contradiction. |
| C | Exclude every sufficiently large fully force-visible lexicographic survivor, retaining isolates | Post-ZF rigidity and topology are not consequences merely of restored PSD. |

The first bridge under examination is:

```text
A Section 155: every global source hull lies in a nearly radius-D/2 disk
  + B: full-source packing/area/perimeter control
  + C: actual length-D chords and their force-hull endpoints
  -> simultaneous control of all diameter midpoints
  -> an approximate centrally symmetric model of the actual force hull
  -> stronger force-hull area and external-population restrictions.
```

The immediate concrete theorem target is a finite Hausdorff bound between the hull
of actual diameter endpoints and the centered polygon generated by their half
diameter vectors. Its area error must be `o(D^2)`. This would improve C's area
constants without identifying the force hull with the full source hull.

A second candidate consequence is that all diameter chords at one endpoint become
parallel asymptotically. If valid, the normalized reciprocal perimeter should tend
to its upper endpoint uniformly over normalized KKT stresses. This would replace
the current fixed-angle ceiling by a vanishing-angle bound.

